fix(trade,transfer,pull-tab): H7 timer + idempotency + listener leak

CRITICAL active trade screen: extension double-counted. _requestTimeExtension
bumped _secondsRemaining locally AND the BE ack time_extended event also
bumped it on arrival. Pressing +15 actually gave +30. Removed the optimistic
local bump; FE waits for the server's time_extended event which carries the
canonical newExpiresAt.

CRITICAL active trade screen: extensions wiped within 1 second.
_recomputeRemaining computed _secondsRemaining = 15min - (now - createdAt)
on every Timer.periodic tick. The screen ignored Trade.expiresAt entirely,
so any extension (correctly persisted on the BE) was overwritten by the FE
recomputation within 1s. Fix: anchor to _tradeExpiresAt sourced from
Trade.expiresAt, with fallback to createdAt + selectedTimeframe for older
BE deploys.

Active trade: message duplication on mid-conversation reload. _onNewMessage
deduped by id, but the history loader didn't include id on loaded entries.
A realtime push landing during the sync round-trip slipped past dedup.
Fixed by including id + createdAt on loaded history entries.

CRITICAL friend transfer: missing idempotency key. FriendService.sendFunds
and requestFunds weren't sending clientRequestId, even though the BE
explicitly supports it for retry safety. Without the key, any retry on a
transient error WAS a fresh debit. Fix: generate a v4-style UUID per call
using Random.secure() and ship it in the body.

Friend transfer: in-flight guard added to _executeTransfer.

Vendor pull-tab: listener leak fixed. _onDragEnd called
_snapController.addListener(...) every drag. Listeners accumulated. After
N drags, the (N+1)th drag fired N setState() calls per animation tick.
Listener now installed ONCE in initState reading _snapAnimation.value.
